  "notes": "The current RSL and RNL records reconcile one exact Russian Antonovsky Edition at Saint Petersburg in 1900 through the shared rc\\1717107 control core, identical 20061002170739.0 transaction value, and matching title, responsibility, year, and 624-page main extent while preserving their distinct literal identifier wrappers. RSL records FB Рб 18/414 and OMF 810-83/174-7 (1900, ч. 1-4); RNL records one current holding, 128/318. The current Lithuanian National Library record identifies the same title, responsibility, place, year, and 624-page main extent under call number 1.40686, but reports [s.n.] and [3], XI rather than RSL/RNL's тип. Б.М. Вольфа and [4], XII. The exact copy/issue relationship, source-visible title and provision wording, and cause of the preliminary-page discrepancy therefore remain unresolved. All four remote holdings are not ToS Items. No record-specific digital object, source pages, or bytes were acquired. Neither [s.n.] nor the literal typography string is converted into a publisher or provision-activity claim. No exemplar identity, responsibility, textual equivalence, derivation, rights, or semantic claim is created.",
  "record_version": 2,
  "supersedes_ref": null
